acceptance_criteria: "package lock manifest and self-reported extension version align with pm CLI/SDK 2026.8.7 and current pm-changelog; pm merge install emits extensions/** -merge followed by the managed-manifest pm-json override; pm-starter-ejr6 receives complete metadata and is closed only after the real service override and fresh installed-CLI output remain correct; every executable TypeScript source remains at exact 100/100/100 coverage; npm and Bun release gates, full and production audits, dependency freshness, package dry-run, changelog, pm validate, and strict check-only health pass; changed files and reachable history are audited for private data and independent blockers are tracked; exact-head PR review completes with no unresolved findings; no publication occurs"
definition_of_ready: "Canonical checkout is clean on released main, no open PR or GitHub issue duplicates the work, installed pm 2026.8.7 is available, and only one local checkout exists"
value: Keep the canonical extension reference safe for agents copying its service and merge patterns
impact: Prevents new packages from inheriting an unsafe output override or stale multi-agent merge fence
outcome: pm-starter demonstrates the current service-decline contract and pm 2026.8.7 package baseline
why_now: Companion critical item pm-cli-website-19ju lists pm-starter among four remaining fleet drifts while its only open package issue is already implemented but not lifecycle-complete
