notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T17:25:24.803Z","harness:codex",Dependency and merge-fence implementation is complete. package.json and package-lock resolve @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.7 and pm-changelog 2026.8.7; .gitattributes ends with extensions/** -merge followed by the managed-manifest pm-json exception. npm and Bun each executed 142 tests at exact 100/100/100 for index.ts and scripts/coverage-gate.ts. A packed pm-starter-2026.8.7 artifact installed into a fresh pm 2026.8.7 tracker; pm list preserved the one real seeded item before and after activation and starter greet returned Hello Agent. Explicit any annotations and dynamic imports were removed from TypeScript tests. Broader fail-closed docstring and source-quality gating is independently tracked as pm-starter-qu97.
  "2026-08-07T17:29:39.759Z","harness:codex",Implementation commit a876dbe opened as PR #54. The PR is intentionally not a publication approval; npm release remains blocked by maintainer approval and pm-starter-asud.
  "2026-08-07T17:31:36.508Z","harness:codex","Initial CI run 31202559000 passed PM health,typecheck,build drift,exact coverage,production audit and package contents on Node 22 and 26,then failed changelog verification. The workflow already fetched full history and tags; the local clone had not fetched v2026.08.07,so local generation incorrectly placed the post-release closed issue under 2026.8.7. After git fetch --force --tags,pm-changelog correctly generated an Unreleased section matching CI. No workflow change was required."
  "2026-08-07T17:39:01.368Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review evidence completed on 4e09f94: CI run 31202997780 passed Node 22 and 26; Greptile reviewed the exact commit at 5/5 with no blocking failure; CodeRabbit's sole actionable security finding was fixed through pm update,verified fail-closed,upvoted,answered inline,confirmed by the bot and resolved. CodeRabbit's requested reruns were quota-limited,Sourcery and Cubic were quota/skipped,and Gemini did not respond; none is treated as approval."
